{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:aborted.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links/doc:flow-control.9", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:more.u1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Divergence, on the credit an aborted delivery spends.** The receiver granted one delivery of credit. `aborted` is a boolean whose value here is *false*, so the delivery is not an aborted one and it consumes the credit the receiver granted \u2014 which makes the second delivery exceed the delivery-limit and be refused. The specification refuses it with `amqp:connection:framing-error` and class `limit`, leaving the peer in `session:MAPPED`; the reference **admits** it, because its `aborted` check is a presence test that reads an explicit false as an abort and returns before the credit block. So the divergence has two causes at once \u2014 the flag's value read as its presence, and the credit an aborted delivery does or does not spend \u2014 and the vector's second step is what separates them from the outside", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000001005312c00903a1046c696e6b4341", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "limit", "state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "refused"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 1}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}], "vector": "staged-link-aborted-false-spends-no-credit"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:aborted.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links/doc:flow-control.9", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links.33"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Divergence, with the flag the clauses do agree about.** Here the delivery really is aborted, so both artefacts discard it \u2014 and they still disagree about the credit it spent. The specification refuses the next delivery with `amqp:connection:framing-error` and class `limit`; the reference **admits** it. Which reading the artifact gives is not stated: `flow-control.5` ties `link-credit` to `delivery-count`, an aborted delivery advances the sender's sequence number, and `aborted.1` requires the *recipient* to discard the message rather than the sender to un-send it. The register is silent, which is why this is staged rather than decided", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000001005312c00903a1046c696e6b4341", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:connection:framing-error", "reason": "limit", "state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "refused"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 1}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}], "vector": "staged-link-aborted-spends-the-credit"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:settled.6", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.5", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** The peer's attach negotiated the `unsettled` choice of `sender-settle-mode`, and `settled.6` says the flag \"MUST be false (or unset) on every transfer frame for a delivery\" under that choice. **Both artefacts admit** this frame and leave the peer in `session:MAPPED`: neither reads the `unsettled` choice anywhere. The clause is disposed `deferred:S4`, and `Contracts/Settlement.lean`'s own closing section states that only the sender's `settled` obligation has a proposition \u2014 but the two artefacts enforcing the `settled` choice's MUST while ignoring the `unsettled` choice's MUST NOT is exactly the declared-against-negotiated shape the sweep was pointed at", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005312c0110aa1046c696e6b43425000404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000004d02000001005314c00a054343a003746167434161206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-settled-over-unsettled-negotiation"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:settled.6", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap, in the direction the sender owns.** Our own attach negotiated `unsettled`, so `settled.6` forbids the flag on the transfers *we* write \u2014 the obligation is the sending end's, and a conformant endpoint withholds the frame rather than being told about it. **Both artefacts write it**: each admits the step and leaves the peer in `session:MAPPED`. The receive-direction vector above says the same about the peer's frames; this one says it about ours, which is where an enforcement would have to live to stop the frame", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "ubyte", "value": 0}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000001005312c00903a1046c696e6b4341", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "refused"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}], "vector": "staged-link-settled-over-unsettled-negotiation-sent"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:settled.4", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.5", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap: the flag's content against its presence.** `settled.4` requires the field to be **true** on at least one transfer of a delivery when the negotiated mode is the `settled` choice. This transfer carries the field with the value *false*, so no transfer of the delivery is settled and the delivery breaks the negotiation \u2014 while both artefacts **admit** it, because both read the flag by presence (`fieldSet`/`present` are true for any non-null value). The corpus already carries the vector where the flag is absent, which both refuse correctly; this is the neighbouring input that shows the check is on the field's shape rather than on its content", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005312c0110aa1046c696e6b43425001404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000004d02000001005314c00a054343a003746167434261206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-settled-false-under-settled-negotiation"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links.29", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-tag.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap, the same shape as the settled flag.** `links.29` says how a split message is carried \u2014 \"by setting the more flag on all but the last \u00abtransfer\u00bb frame\" \u2014 so a transfer whose `more` is *false* is the last one and the delivery it carries is complete. Both artefacts **admit** both steps here: they read `more` by presence, so an explicit false continues the delivery and the following continuation, which has nothing to continue, is admitted too. The second step is what makes the reading observable rather than a matter of taste: whichever way the flag is read, the two steps cannot both be right", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000004e02000001005314c00b064343a00374616743404261206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000004502000001005314c002014361206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-more-false-completes-the-delivery"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:rcv-settle-mode.u1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:attach/field:rcv-settle-mode.1", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.5", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** `rcv-settle-mode.u1` says that \"If the negotiated link value is \u00abfirst\u00bb, then it is illegal to set this field to \u00absecond\u00bb\" \u2014 the attach fixed the link at `first`, and this transfer names `second`. **Both artefacts admit** it: neither reads the transfer's `rcv-settle-mode` at all, and neither reads the attach's. The corpus's conforming vector for the negotiation (`exchange-session-attach-defaults-admitted`) cites the attach field, so the transfer-side rule has been cited and never exercised", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "ubyte", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000005002000001005314c00d074343a003746167434040500161206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-rcv-settle-second-over-first"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:flow/field:delivery-count.3", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:links/doc:flow-control.3"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** `flow/field:delivery-count.3` requires a flow sent from the receiver to the sender to carry \"the last known value of the corresponding sending endpoint\". This endpoint is the link's sender and has sent one delivery, so the receiver's flow reporting zero is naming a value the sending endpoint never had. **Both artefacts admit** it, and the specification's own disposition says so in terms: `.3` \"is not carried at all\", because its selector asks which end *issued* the frame and returns `none` for the receiver's flows. The corpus's admitted half (`exchange-flow-receiver-count-echoed`) is the delimitation", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000001005312c00903a1046c696e6b4341", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-flow-receiver-count-not-echoed"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:flow/field:delivery-count.2", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.5", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:sessions.6"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap: the presence half of a sentence whose value half is enforced.** `flow/field:delivery-count.2` requires the field to be set, not only to be right, and this flow names the link and omits it entirely. **Both artefacts admit** it: the specification's guard is a match on a present field and falls through when it is absent, which the disposition for `.2` records as the half its carrier misses, and the reference returns early on an absent count. `exchange-flow-sender-count-not-its-current` pins the half both do enforce, so the two together give the clause both readings", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001b02000001005313c00e054370000003e84370000003e843", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-flow-sender-count-absent"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:resume.2", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** `transfer/field:resume.2`: \"The sender MUST NOT send resumed transfers for deliveries not in its local unsettled map.\" Our endpoint is the link's sender and has sent nothing, so a resumed transfer for delivery zero is a resume of a delivery that does not exist. **Both artefacts write it**: neither reads the `resume` field, which the specification's disposition records as uncarried (`deferred:S4`) and the reference's layer never mentions. The clause is stated for the sending end, so this is one a conformance check could hold without an unsettled map \u2014 the map's absence is what makes the delivery's absence easy to state and impossible to check", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": false}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001602000001005312c00903a1046c696e6b4341", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001e02000001005313c011074370000003e84370000003e843435201", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"direction": "send", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "refused"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 20}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"hex": "746167", "type": "binary"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "null"}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "payload": "61206d6573736167652077686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "type": "00"}}], "vector": "staged-link-resume-sent-not-in-map"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:resume.3", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:transfer/field:delivery-tag.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** `resume.3`: \"If a resumed delivery spans more than one transfer performative, then the resume flag MUST be set to true on the *first* transfer of the resumed delivery.\" The delivery here is resumed \u2014 its continuation says so \u2014 while the first transfer that began it did not. **Both artefacts admit** both steps. The corpus's admitted half (`exchange-link-resume-on-first-transfer`) has the flag where the clause requires it, and the pair is what separates \"the flag is read\" from \"the flag is required in a place\"", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005312c0100aa1046c696e6b434240404040404043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000001d02000001005313c010074370000003e84370000003e8434343", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000002202000001005314c00b064343a00374616743404161206d65737361676520", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}}, {"bytes": "0000004302000001005314c00a0943404040404040404177686f73652073706c697420706f696e7473206172652074686520766563746f72277320627573696e657373", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-resume-only-on-continuation"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:attach/field:unsettled.5", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:performatives/type:attach/field:snd-settle-mode.1"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap.** `attach/field:unsettled.5`: \"The unsettled map MUST NOT contain null valued keys.\" A null key is a legal map key in the type system \u2014 which is why the clause has to forbid it *here* \u2014 and the reference decodes this frame happily. **Both artefacts admit** it: neither reads the `unsettled` field at all, and the specification's disposition records the generated table row as the field's only trace. The map itself is well formed (an even item count, a null key, an octet-string value), so the only rule this frame breaks is the one the vector names", "start": "session:MAPPED", "steps": [{"direction": "send", "expect": {"state": "session:MAPPED", "status": "admitted"}, "value": {"body": [{"descriptor": {"type": "ulong", "value": 18}, "type": "described", "value": {"items": [{"text": "link", "type": "string"}, {"type": "uint", "value": 0}, {"type": "boolean", "value": true}], "type": "list"}}], "channel": 1, "doff": 2, "type": "00"}}, {"bytes": "0000002302000001005312c0160aa1046c696e6b434240404040c1050240a001004043", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:invalid-field", "reason": "malformed", "state": "session:DISCARDING", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-link-attach-unsettled-null-key"}
{"clauses": ["amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#picture.24", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:framing.4", "amqp-core-transport-v1.0-os.xml#amqp:transport/section:connections/doc:doc-idle-time-out.7"], "kind": "exchange", "note": "**Shared gap: a frame with no body defeats the table's `-` column.** `picture.24` gives END `-` in both columns, and the corpus already pins that a `close` and a protocol header arriving there are refused with `amqp:illegal-state` and class `illegalState`. A frame whose header is all there is \u2014 which `framing.4` licenses, and which `doc-idle-time-out.10` forbids *sending* after a close \u2014 is **admitted by both artefacts in END**, with no state change, because both short-circuit on a bodyless frame before the state column is consulted. The idle-timeout clause requires a peer to handle empty frames \"on any valid channel\"; it does not license one on a connection that is over, and the table's `-` is what says so", "start": "connection:END", "steps": [{"bytes": "0000000802000000", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:illegal-state", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "connection:END", "status": "refused"}, "note": "END's legal receives are `-`, so a frame arrives where the table admits none"}, {"bytes": "0000000802000001", "direction": "receive", "expect": {"condition": "amqp:illegal-state", "reason": "illegalState", "state": "connection:END", "status": "refused"}}], "vector": "staged-bodyless-frame-in-end"}
